  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule now exist in Kibana. I could not run the queries against the data itself, so the panels and the rule have not been checked against real results.\n\n**Data exploration:** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) holds request-level web logs. The fields that matter here are `clientip`, `bytes`, `response` (with a `response.keyword` subfield for exact matching), `extension`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, and `timestamp`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-de2fd138 Web logs overview`**\n- ID: `eff-de2fd138-web-logs-overview-bee2aab71637`\n- Six panels, all on the logs data view:\n  - Total requests (count)\n  - Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n  - Average response size in bytes (average of `bytes`)\n  - Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n  - Responses by status code (pie, terms on `response.keyword`)\n  - Top requested extensions (bar, terms on `extension.keyword`)\n- Time range: last 7 days. I chose this myself; the sample data may sit outside that window.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-de2fd138 5xx spike`**\n- ID: `6f26ec71-5be5-403d-b1a5-4f44727f9869`\n- Type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, schedule every 1 minute.\n- Condition: count of documents with `response.keyword` matching `5*` in a 5-minute window, fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- I enabled it so it actually runs every minute. Its current status is `pending`, and it has no action connector, so a firing will not notify anyone yet.\n\n**Open items:**\n- The `/api/esql/query` and console proxy endpoints returned 404 and 400, so I could not inspect the live distinct `response` values. The 5xx match uses a wildcard on the keyword field, which should be correct for the sample data.\n- Once the rule has run, it's worth checking that it evaluates without errors.",
